= <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> Conference

[? if marcher_break_toleration: Due to the breaking of our toleration agreement toward the [+ chancellor +] government, the right wing of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> finally has enough strength and anger toward the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> to oust the friendly Hawkins as leader. ?]

[? if unionist_relation < 40 and not marcher_break_toleration: Due to the worsening of our relationship, even with Hawkins at the helm, the right wing of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> finally has enough power to oust the friendly Hawkins as leader. ?]

[? if concordat_explode and not marcher_break_toleration and unionist_relation >= 40: Due to our lack of progress toward an agreement with the Temple of the Faithful, the clerical wing of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> has forced Hawkins's resignation for his unwillingness to force the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> to take action. ?]

[? if secularized_a or abortion_rights or homosexual_rights and not concordat_explode and not marcher_break_toleration and unionist_relation >= 40: Due to our progress on rights for women and <span style="color: red;">Ho</span><span style="color: orange;">m</span><span style="color: yellow;">ox</span><span style="color: green;">se</span><span style="color: blue;">ua</span><span style="color: purple;">ls</span>, the clerical wing of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> has forced Hawkins from the chairmanship, citing his unwillingness to obstruct these changes. ?]

Aurelian Renck, a devoted Faithful priest is expected to succeed him, but Adam Sedgewick is once again running for the party's leadership. 

- @kaas: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] elects Aurelian Renck as the party chair.
- @stegerwald: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] elects Adam Sedgewick as the party chair.

@kaas
view-if: not heartland_leader == "Sedgewick" and ((marcher_in_government_time >= 36 and (not reichskonkordat_progress and in_weimar_coalition and foreign_minister_party == "Marcher")) or (marcher_heartland_time >= 30 and not heartland_concordat_progress))
on-arrival: unionist_leader = "Renck"; unionist_relation -= 5; heartland_concordat_progress += 1; unionist_ideology = "Right"
face-image: img/portraits/Ludwig_Renck.jpg

Aurelian Renck has been selected as the chairman of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. He represents a rightward turn from Hawkins, and will preside over a [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] less inclined to compromise with the left. 

Despite this, Renck is committed to the current constitutional order and the republic. He maintains a close friendship with Eugenio Pacelli, the Papal Nuncio to the Commonwealth, which may prove useful during concordat negotiations.

@stegerwald
choose-if: heartland_leader == "Sedgewick" or not concordat_explode
unavailable-subtitle: [? if heartland_leader != "Sedgewick": Sedgewick lacks the influence necessary to have a real chance. ?][? if ((marcher_in_government_time >= 36 and (not reichskonkordat_progress and in_weimar_coalition and foreign_minister_party == "Marcher")) or (marcher_heartland_time >= 30 and not heartland_concordat_progress)): The clerical wing of the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> would much rather elect one of their own. ?]
on-arrival: unionist_leader = "Sedgewick"; stegerwald_transformation_timer = 12; unionist_ideology = "Right"; stegerwald_path = 1; unionist_relation -= 8; zentrum_disintegration += 2; burgher_unionist -= 5; guild_unionist -= 3; landed_unionist -= 1; faithful_unionist -= 5; commons_unionist += 5; disfavored_unionist += 3; faithful_marcher += 8; faithful_other += 4; faithful_traditionalist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; faithful_gold += 4; faithful_ddp += 2; faithful_lvp += 4; gold_right += 1; ddp_left += 1; ddp_cohesion += 1; liberal_cooperation += 1; bourgeois_cooperation += 1; faithful -= 5; burgher_traditionalist -= 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; guild_traditionalist -= 3 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; landed_traditionalist -= 3 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; burgher_unionist += 2 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; guild_unionist += 3 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; landed_unionist += 3 if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if heartland_leader == "Sedgewick"
face-image: img/portraits/stegerwald.jpg

Adam Sedgewick has been elected as the chairman of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. He seems to represent a rightward turn from Vael, despite his Free Guild background, and will preside over a [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] less inclined to compromise with the left. He views the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] as a prototype for a <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span>, <span style="color: #586593;">democratic</span>, <span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth</span>, and <span style="color: #c00000;">social</span> party, and aims to transform it according to the principles laid out in his proposed "Ashford program" eight years prior. 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]'s middle class wing are in uproar over the vote, despite Sedgewick conceding his leadership of the Assembly delegation and the Minister-Presidency to his protege Edmund Askew. [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": His election also attracts some dissenting <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> dissidents and guild-masters, who may result in a shift of the party towards the right. ?]